To find the total number of spiders over 80 years at a rate of 8 spiders per year, multiply the annual rate by the number of years:

\[
8 \text{ spiders/year} \times 80 \text{ years} = 640 \text{ spiders}
\]

**Answer:**  
\boxed{640}

